      "final_text": "\n\nAll done and verified \u2014 the tool worked correctly on the first run, so no debugging was needed.\n\n## What was created\n\n- **`tools/minidiff.py`** \u2014 dependency-free Python 3 (stdlib `difflib` only) word-level diff CLI. It aligns the files line-by-line, then word-by-word within changed line pairs; output is unified style with 1 line of context, only changed hunks printed, substituted words shown inline as `-old +new`, and whole-line insertions/deletions as plain `+`/`-` lines. Exit codes: 1 if any difference, 0 if identical, 2 on usage/I-O errors.\n- **`a.txt`** \u2014 5 lines of lighthouse prose.\n- **`b.txt`** \u2014 same prose with exactly 3 single-word substitutions: `old`\u2192`ancient`, `wick`\u2192`lamp`, `light`\u2192`glow`.\n\n## Verification results\n\n- `python3 tools/minidiff.py a.txt b.txt` \u2192 **exit 1**, output contains all 3 substituted words (`ancient`, `lamp`, `glow` \u2014 confirmed via grep).\n- `python3 tools/minidiff.py a.txt a.txt` \u2192 **exit 0**, zero bytes of output.\n- Edge test (word insertion + whole-line deletion) \u2192 correct inline `delta +omega`, `-lambda mu nu`, two properly separated hunks with correct `@@` headers, exit 1.\n- No arguments \u2192 usage message on stderr, exit 2.\n\n## Exact diff output between the two fixtures\n\n```\n--- a.txt\n+++ b.txt\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n The -old +ancient lighthouse stood on the black cliffs.\n Its beam swept the dark water every night.\n Keeper Marlow trimmed the -wick +lamp at dawn.\n Fog rolled in from the north each spring.\n Ships followed the steady -light +glow to harbor.\n```"
